From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/kms: suspend without the PM console VT switch

kernel/power/console.c switches to the suspend console on every system
suspend unless a registered device says pm_vt_switch_required(dev, false).
register_framebuffer() normally does that, but the ROG5 boots without an
fbdev client, so every suspend switched VTs. That deactivated the graphical
seat session: seatd disabled Denial (which then never re-added its libinput
devices, so touch and keys were dead after a wake), and logind paused phoc,
which re-created DSI-1 on resume and crashed phosh.

The compositors restore the display themselves, so msm KMS registers that the
switch is not required. Verified on SM8350 with the same call from an
out-of-tree module: s2idle suspend and power-key wake keep the phosh session
active, no seat pause, touch and keys work.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_kms.c	2026-09-27 01:49:39.342280351 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_kms.c	2026-09-27 01:49:39.355586391 +0200
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/aperture.h>
 #include <linux/kthread.h>
+#include <linux/pm.h>
 #include <linux/sched/mm.h>
 #include <uapi/linux/sched/types.h>
 
@@ -256,6 +257,8 @@
 	msm_irq_uninstall(ddev);
 	pm_runtime_put_sync(dev);
 
+	pm_vt_switch_unregister(dev);
+
 	if (kms && kms->funcs)
 		kms->funcs->destroy(kms);
 }
@@ -333,6 +336,14 @@
 
 	drm_mode_config_reset(ddev);
 
+	/*
+	 * Userspace compositors restore the display after resume, so the PM
+	 * core does not need to switch to the suspend console. Without an
+	 * fbdev client nothing else says so, and the VT switch deactivated the
+	 * seat session on every suspend.
+	 */
+	pm_vt_switch_required(dev, false);
+
 	return 0;
 
 err_msm_uninit:
